From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Wed Jun 3 00:00:00 2026
From: Carl Su <xuyusu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tools: pkcs11-tool: use _Static_assert

pkcs11-tool uses static_assert without including a header that provides
it as a macro.  With uClibc, this leaves static_assert undeclared, so the
compiler emits a call to an implicit function and the link fails with:

  undefined reference to `static_assert'

Use the C11 _Static_assert keyword directly.  The configure script already
checks for _Static_assert support and the affected toolchains support it,
so this avoids relying on libc header support for the static_assert macro.

Signed-off-by: Carl Su <xuyusu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Upstream: Not submitted
---
 src/tools/pkcs11-tool.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/tools/pkcs11-tool.c b/src/tools/pkcs11-tool.c
index 9404affaf..a9c2652dd 100644
--- a/src/tools/pkcs11-tool.c
+++ b/src/tools/pkcs11-tool.c
@@ -844,7 +844,7 @@ int main(int argc, char * argv[])
 	char *s = NULL;
 	CK_RV rv;
 
-	static_assert(sizeof(options) / sizeof(options[0]) == sizeof(option_help) / sizeof(option_help[0]),
+	_Static_assert(sizeof(options) / sizeof(options[0]) == sizeof(option_help) / sizeof(option_help[0]),
 			"Inconsistent size of the options and options_help structures!");
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
-- 
